cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Understanding Open Source Software Licensing"
message: >-
  Please cite this lesson using the information in this file
  when you refer to it in publications, and/or if you
  re-use, adapt, or expand on the content in your own
  training material.
type: dataset
authors:
  - given-names: Karla
    family-names: Padilla
  - given-names: Jose
    family-names: Niño Muriel
  - given-names: Laura
    family-names: Langdon
  - given-names: Reid
    family-names: Otsuji
repository-code: "https://github.com/UC-OSPO-Network/oss-license-workshop"
abstract: >-
  A UC OSPO Network lesson on open source software licensing.
  It is for people who write or share code and are unsure which
  license to choose, and for anyone curious about how open source
  licenses work. Learners describe what a license is, compare
  permissive and copyleft licenses, recognize when the licenses of
  a project's dependencies clash, and choose a license for an
  example project.
license: CC-BY-4.0
